```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{chessboard}

\begin{document}

\begin{figure}[h]
\centering
\chessboard[FEN="your_fen_here"]
\caption{Chessboard state represented by the FEN notation: \texttt{your_fen_here}}
\label{fig:chessboard}
\end{figure}

\end{document}
```

Here's a breakdown of what the code does:

- `\documentclass{article}`: Sets up the document class.
- `\usepackage{chessboard}`: Imports the `chessboard` package.
- `\begin{document}`: Begins the document content.
- `\begin{figure}[h]`: Starts a floating figure environment to center the chessboard image.
- `\centering`: Centers the figure on

